# Project Configuration for OpenManusWeb

## Tech Stack
- FastAPI for backend web server
- Python 3.12 as core programming language
- WebSocket for real-time communication
- SQLite for session storage and persistence
- Vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript for frontend
- xterm.js for terminal emulation
- OpenAI API for LLM interactions
- Asyncio for concurrent operations

## Project Structure
/app
  /web          # Web interface components
    /app.py     # Main FastAPI application
    /static     # Frontend assets and JS files
    /templates  # HTML templates
    /thinking_tracker.py # AI thinking steps tracking
    /session_storage.py  # Session persistence
  /agent        # Agent implementations
    /base.py    # Base agent class
    /manus.py   # Manus agent implementation
  /flow         # Flow controllers
    /planning.py # Planning-based execution flow
  /tool         # Tool implementations
  /utils        # Utility functions
/logs           # Log files
/workspace      # Files generated by the AI

## Implementation Guidelines
- WebSocket updates should be incremental to reduce network traffic
- Use step_id deduplication for thinking steps to avoid duplicates
- Follow established two-pane layout matching Manus AI product
- Add detailed logging for debugging complex interactions
- Implement proper error handling for API rate limits

## Development Workflow
- Focus on fixing execution loop issue (steps getting stuck at 4)
- Follow modular development with clear separation of concerns
- Use ThinkingTracker for visualizing AI reasoning process
- Comprehensive debugging for complex async operations
- Test frequently with live requests to verify WebSocket stability

## Security
DO NOT read or modify:
- .env files
- Config files containing API keys
- Authentication credentials
- User data stored in SQLite databases
- Any file containing OpenAI API keys

## Current Priorities
1. Fix execution loop issue in planning.py
2. Enhance terminal integration with better output handling
3. Improve step details display in the thinking timeline
4. Implement session replay functionality
5. Add comprehensive error handling